 while this matrix sat in analysis under its eighth changes-requested verdict. This is the verdict-05 F2 class one field over: verdict 05 checked what a consumer SAYS, rules A1/P1 check which revision it NAMES, and nothing checked WHEN it runs - A1/P1 only cover the two consumers carrying a revision label, and for every other consumer a missing edge fails silently because nothing reads a prose list. Four more elements carrying obligations were absent from consumers entirely, three of them assigned from inside PROSE fields (legacy.migrationDecisionOwner named TASK-260715-35nc5m for eight revisions; two sentences named TASK-260717-xempiv for five), which is why D1's derived set scans every string in the contract rather than three named lists. Fix: ONE board edge, 29ws8l blocked by this task, cycle-checked over the whole graph first - it orders all three because 29ws8l already blocks the other two, and it is semantically real, since 29ws8l AC2 specifies App Group and providerConfiguration data and AC4 specifies Keychain accessibility and access group, exactly what G4 and K2 decide. Gate R37 plus a new D1 block in check-portal-consumer.py reading blockedBy for tasks AND bugs make a missing edge fail closed; reachability is transitive; done is explicitly NOT an exemption basis because having finished is evidence a consumer RAN, which is the failure D1 catches; the one upstream exemption is verified upstream rather than accepted. RULE N1: the other half of the count class r6 left open - section 9.1 records it biting already, r3's prose claiming a number over a list holding a different one, r4 correcting it by hand, r5 moving it again when K2 withdrew the keychain group, while r6's scan covers App Group RECORD counts only. N1 derives allowlist counts and the rendered key list from the rows in both artifacts, pins its exclusion lists because widening an exclusion is the quiet way to neuter a scan, and states its bound rather than implying completeness. Three defects in the NEW gates were found by their own negative mutations and fixed rather than worked around: R37's reverse check was TAUTOLOGICAL because it counted the consumers list itself as a mention, so appending a consumer id present nowhere else passed; a graph mutation premised on cutting 3jloqy's edge orphaned nothing because q5kjta also blocks it and carries its own edge, so the premise was wrong rather than the gate, and it is also the argument for a closure over an edge check; and a document mutation did not apply against a hard-wrapped sentence. The fixed reverse check immediately found TASK-260715-33oofa - a declared consumer the contract never explained, its obligation stated inside the macOS task's entry while 33oofa is the iOS half carrying the opposite instruction - now recorded. Also recorded, not smoothed over: the board resource store does not preserve the executable bit, so a re-registered .sh exits 126 on a ./ run and must be invoked via zsh. Gates: validate_matrix.py 37 rules 2483 checks exit 0; mutate.py 202/202 negative gates exit 0 (38 new - 20 D1, 18 N1 - including a new dependency-GRAPH harness, because D1's reachability half cannot be tested by corrupting the contract, which is why eight revisions of a 1331-check validator never saw it); check-portal-consumer.py 84 checks over 3 rules exit 0; preserve.py 122 assertions exit 0, including a top-level check that the only keys ADDED are consumerDependencyContract and numericClaimContract and the only keys CHANGED are revision, supersedes, revisionLog, consumers and downstreamConsequences; an independent gate that imports no project harness flips r8 false/exit 1 to r9 true/exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. All four matrix harnesses re-verified running in place from the board resource layout; every command run without a pipeline because zsh carries no PIPESTATUS. No entitlement decision, target row, profile row, record, assertion, assertion scope or C1 mutation set changed. Board footprint: one dependency edge added, and one field on one element - TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope, revision label r8 to r9, character delta 0, verified byte-exact, required by amendmentRule. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-scoped; no portal mutation; no product source, spec file or generated project touched. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-ae0e2a, pid=3124, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c)\nReviewer verdict 08 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, route analysis. Blocking F1: the matrix permanently omits a /Library/Keychains sandbox file exception using only macOS 26.5 application.sb evidence, while the binding generated-target floor is macOS 15.0. No OS-version constraint or reopening rule covers sandbox-policy drift, so automated allowlists could reject an entitlement required on a supported floor. Verify the grant and securityd lookups on macOS 15/oldest supported runtime or model the version-specific uncertainty, extend K1/X1 and negative gates, and attach durable r8 input if preserve.py remains claimed. Evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-08.md. Independent exits: validator 0 (2483), mutations 0 (202/202), board consumer 0 (84), reviewer gates 0, legacy 0, board validate 0, swift test 0 (335/29). preserve.py not rerun because r8 input is not attached.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c, pid=26992, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f)\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f, pid=34042, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4)\nReviewer verdict 09 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, route analysis. Blocking F1: r10 pre-authorizes conditional exception X1-C1, but R39 accepts coordinated drift of its exact least-privilege path, signing-channel set, and arming owner. Independent mutations widened /Library/Keychains/ to /, removed developer-id from channelsIfArmed, and changed armedBy from TASK-260715-1uxx3i to TASK-260715-9yp8to; validate-matrix.py exited 0 for all three when each negative control must exit 1. Supplied gates remain green: validator 2654 exit 0, mutations 220/220 exit 0, board A1/P1/D1 exit 0, both preservation gates exit 0, reviewer gates exit 0, legacy exit 0, board validate exit 0, swift test 335/29 exit 0. Full evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-09.md.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4, pid=49397, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-17c375, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-17c375)\nr11 rework against reviewer verdict 09 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1 plus required rework items 2-5). F1 was reproduced before it was accepted, against the UNMODIFIED r10 artifact and with the r10 validator and r10 rationale, because judging r10 data with the r11 gate proves nothing: all three coordinated-drift mutations exited 0 where a negative control must exit 1. CONFIRMED. No entitlement decision, identifier, target row, profile row, record, assertion, assertion scope, open constraint or Ceremony C1 mutation set changed, and X1-C1 itself is byte-for-byte what r10 reviewed - r11 changes how it is CHECKED. Rule X1 gains conditionalExceptionDerivation and R39 now DERIVES every field instead of comparing the register to its own mirror on the row: target from the unique row carrying the K3 version scope, key from K3's arming instruction, value set from a path-subtree bound that no coordinated edit can widen, channel set from the target's own channels in full, arming owner from K3's resolutionOwner cross-checked against the rule-D1 consumer list, review revision from the revision log, scope sentence as a rendered clause. The reviewed path and the bound vocabulary live in the gate, because a bound that lives only inside the data it bounds is not a bound. The item-3 sweep found two more of the same class the verdict had not named - a coordinated TARGET move to macos.host, and a reviewedIn naming a revision never issued - and one that had passed only by accident, key drift, which exited 1 under R35's assertion-scope partition rather than under the rule that owns the register. Item 4 was closed as a class, not as a string: the count was invisible twice over, because rule N1's only shape was '<n> keys' and both live sentences sat in scan-excluded regions, \u00a713 by exclusion and the preamble wholesale. N1 gains the harness-count shape, mutate.py counts its own entries and fails on disagreement, the validator requires the prose to render the declared value, and the preamble is now scanned with historical figures handled as named exclusions with reasons. That immediately surfaced a third stale number one paragraph away: \u00a79.2 claimed 36 internal consistency rules over R1-R36 while the file gates R2-R39 and has never had an R1; it is derived now too. Also found and reported rather than smoothed over: reviewer-gates.sh could not fail - its exit code was the trailing printf's, so it was 0 whatever the gates said, and four verdicts recorded that 0 as evidence; it now accumulates failures and was proved to exit 1 against a deliberately widened contract. r9's declared scan shape had already diverged from the compiled pattern. Two gates crashed instead of failing when their register was deleted; both now report under R38. Item 5 done: board resource metadata refreshed for the JSON, rationale, validator, mutation harness, board gate, both older preservation harnesses and the reviewer gates. Gates: validate-matrix.py 2805 checks exit 0; mutate.py 253/253 negative gates exit 0 with the declared R39 count matching the harness; check-portal-consumer.py 88 checks over 20 declared consumers exit 0; preserve.py 122, preserve-r10.py 201 and new preserve-r11.py 143 assertions exit 0; reviewer-gates.sh flips the r10 baseline false to r11 true and rejects four negative controls, exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. preserve-r11.py was itself proved to fail closed on seven probes. All harnesses re-verified running in place from the board resource layout; the store drops the executable bit so the .sh is run via zsh. Every command run without a pipeline because zsh carries no PIPESTATUS. Board footprint: one field on one element, TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope, revision label r10 to r11, character delta 0, verified byte-exact. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-linked; no dependency edge added; no portal mutation; no product source, spec file or generated project touched. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-17c375, pid=52455, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-c1a5a8, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-c1a5a8)\nReviewer verdict 10 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, route analysis. Blocking F1: R39 accepts X1-C1.reviewedIn=2026-07-28.r2 even though r2 predates the conditional exception and r10 introduced its pre-authorization. Single-field negative control: validate-matrix.py reported 2805 checks PASS and exit 0 where exit 1 naming R39 is required. Supplied exits remain green: validator 0, mutations 253/253 exit 0, board A1/P1/D1 exit 0, preservation gates exit 0, reviewer gates exit 0, legacy exit 0, board validate exit 0, swift test 335/29 exit 0. Evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-10.md.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-c1a5a8, pid=73457, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1e0752, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1e0752)\nr12 rework against reviewer verdict 10 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1). The finding was independently reproduced against the unmodified r11 artifact before acceptance and CONFIRMED: X1-C1.reviewedIn moved from 2026-07-28.r10 to 2026-07-28.r2, validate-matrix.py PASS over 2805 checks, exit 0, where a negative control must exit 1. r11 had already documented this gap under a Stated bound heading in section 4.5 and gated it at membership anyway - writing a gap down is not closing it, which is why the fix is a derivation and not a stricter string. New rule X1-P (exceptionReviewProvenance) derives the revision each register entry first entered this contract in, from evidence older than the claim: snapshot-proven, from the digest-pinned per-revision baselines the preservation harnesses already consume (X1-C1 absent from r8 and r9, present in r10), and summary-attested as a fallback for an entry older than the oldest baseline (X1-A1 attested by r3), refused wherever the chain can decide; both cross-checked against the new revisionLog[].introduces record. The chain is protected against narrowing as well as tampering - contiguous to supersedes, no undeclared baseline left on disk - because dropping the snapshot in which an entry is absent silently demotes it to attestation. known-revision is REMOVED from the implemented bound vocabulary so r11's rejected bound cannot re-enter as a declaration. Beyond the literal ask, the class was closed across BOTH registers: the ACTIVE register was worse and no verdict had reported it, requiring reviewedIn to be non-empty and nothing else, so it accepted 2026-07-28.r99 - and its entry authorises the Sparkle exception that IS in the shipped macOS host bundle. Gate assignment follows register ownership, so verdict 10's own control fails under R39 as required and the active register's under R26. The independent reviewer-gates.sh had been checking the same insufficient predicate, so verdict 10's control passed there too; section 3 now loads the chain from disk, recomputes the digests and derives the introduction itself. Residual bound measured rather than asserted: a fully coordinated baseline+pin+record+entry edit passes the validator and fails preserve.py and preserve-r10.py, both run against a tampered baseline. Gates, all real exit codes, run in place from the board resource layout: validate-matrix.py 2862 checks exit 0; mutate.py 285/285 negative gates exit 0 including four that corrupt a baseline rather than a claim about one; check-portal-consumer.py exit 0; preserve 122/201/143/245 assertions all exit 0; reviewer-gates.sh exit 0 with eight negative controls; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0. swift test is FLAKY on this tree and is reported rather than smoothed over: 3 failures in 24 full runs, all snapshot.activeConnections == 0 in HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests at lines 646 and 333, on a tree where git status over Sources, Tests, Package.swift, Protocol, relay, scripts and .spec was empty for the whole session; raised as BUG-260728-2j25tu under STORY-260715-1nsw9p rather than fixed from a decision-artifact task. Board: TASK-260728-q5kjta scope re-pointed r11 to r12 under rule A1, the revision label being the only edit; a board-wide sweep found exactly that one live record. No entitlement decision, identifier, target row, profile row, record, assertion, assertion scope, open constraint, dependency edge or Ceremony C1 mutation set changed; no product source, spec or generated project modified. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-1e0752, pid=84724, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-ad8159, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-ad8159)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-ad8159, pid=18814, exit=0)
